      "content": "It sounds like your grief is so deep that even words and treatment plans feel insufficient, making you feel trapped in this moment. Your metaphor of being a passenger watching the world fade beautifully captures the profound loss and helplessness many feel when facing a terminal decline. While waiting for the formal permission to rest can be incredibly difficult, here are some gentle steps you can consider taking right now to find some small peace amidst the heaviness. Would you be open to trying one of these methods: focusing on a physical sensation like warmth from your hands, or perhaps writing down everything you want to say to your memories before you can move on? Sometimes finding an outlet allows us to hold onto pieces of ourselves even when the body and time seem to be slipping away.",
